# Latest frozen candidate: adaptive-consistent

**Use adaptive-consistent-assembly.npz**, SHA256 `712a550fbbb56090ae700e30e4e21153d04c16139062ebcd2a72e818f3e34f7b`, for independent review. The earlier adaptive-final remains frozen below for comparison.

After independent review identified the coupling between offset directions and obstacle support constraints, one additional constrained solve used the previous final directors and a0.21mm construction target. All six support-plane distances measured against the resulting FINAL geometry now exceed0.2mm: minimum0.2123017mm, remaining0.5823656,0.6077466,2.2506130,2.5207035,2.5338586mm. These are six local signed support-plane constraints, **not** a global clearance certificate.

Gate remains zero crossings and all topology checks pass. Center displacement maximum19.0240631mm, p95 over285 pairs8.9685943mm, shell maximum19.4577463mm. All120 moved centers, source preservation, original thickness and zero mixed/nonpositive director products remain as below. adaptive-consistent-build.json includes measured final constraints; adaptive-consistent-preservation.json confirms exact fixed geometry. No visual/game approval.

Reproduce this extra solve with build_consistent_clearance.py, FIDELITY=.133352143, PREFIX=consistent-1, PRIOR=fidelity-0p133-midfield.npz, OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1. The adaptive-consistent assembly copies consistent-1 geometry and adds the measured build/provenance string. Its gate and sampled source-distance reports are separate.

